  "raw_meta_yaml": "schema_version: 1\n\ncontext:\n  version: \"0.1.9\"\n\npackage:\n  name: libsqlite-vec\n  version: ${{ version }}\n\nsource:\n  url: https://github.com/asg017/sqlite-vec/archive/refs/tags/v${{ version }}.tar.gz\n  sha256: 9823e737d9934dcbe85dff75d3fca81018a9beee803d70fa77b16faab5d61dc9\n  patches:\n    - 0001-respect-build-flags.patch\n    - 0002-avoid-using-uv-in-tests.patch\n\nbuild:\n  number: 0\n\nrequirements:\n  build:\n    - ${{ stdlib(\"c\") }}\n    - ${{ compiler('c') }}\n    - gettext  # envsubst for sqlite-vec.h generation\n    - if: unix\n      then: make\n    - if: win\n      then:\n        - m2-bash\n        - m2-coreutils\n        - m2-sed\n        - m2-make\n  host:\n    - libsqlite\n  # sqlite-vec use sqlite's table interface API, not a linked libsqlite.\n  ignore_run_exports:\n    by_name:\n      - libsqlite\n\ntests:\n  - script: bash run_test.sh\n    files:\n      source:\n        - tests/\n        - Makefile\n      recipe:\n        - run_test.sh\n    requirements:\n      run:\n        - python >=3.12\n        - pytest\n        - numpy\n        - syrupy\n        - if: unix\n          then: make\n        - if: win\n          then:\n            - m2-bash\n            - m2-coreutils\n            - m2-sed\n            - m2-make\n\nabout:\n  homepage: https://github.com/asg017/sqlite-vec\n  summary: SQLite loadable extension for vector search\n  description: |\n    sqlite-vec is a SQLite loadable extension providing vector search\n    functionality through the vec0 virtual table and vec_* SQL functions.\n  license: MIT OR Apache-2.0\n  license_file:\n    - LICENSE-MIT\n    - LICENSE-APACHE\n  repository: https://github.com/asg017/sqlite-vec\n  documentation: https://alexgarcia.xyz/sqlite-vec/\n\nextra:\n  recipe-maintainers:\n    - jsmolic\n",
